 "s2_filled": {
  "rule": "Radar + Sentinel-2 tier, published next to the radar-only totals and never replacing them; the area it adds is measured by Sentinel-2, not by the radar. Green = the field's median seasonal-maximum NDVI above 0.40 (s2_winter_active over 1 Nov-15 Mar, s2_summer_active over 10 Jun-31 Oct). (a) Winter fill: a field the radar calls not farmed in any season it observed (radar idle: winter observed and not active, summer not active or not observed) that Sentinel-2 sees green over 1 Nov-15 Mar and not green over 10 Jun-31 Oct counts as winter-farmed (audit nd-8). Fields the radar sees farmed in summer are not filled. (b) Outside the Arabian Shield, the season the radar did not observe on a partly-seen field takes the Sentinel-2 flag for that season. (c) Outside the Shield, fields with no usable radar season (radar not usable, or outside the swath) are classified from the two Sentinel-2 flags alone, a separate tier. Every mapped field is green in at least one window (the field mask is Sentinel-2 green), so (c) counts all of its fields as farmed: an upper bound for them. (d) A filled field farmed in both seasons gets the year-round (perennial) depth only if the spring check marks it perennial (not brown over 20 Apr-5 Jun) and Sentinel-2 sees it green in both windows; otherwise it is a rotation (winter plus summer depth). Palm groves among the filled fields: tree cover of 30% or more, farmed in every known season and not brown in spring; radar palm groves are never refilled. (e) Wheat straw on fields that are wheat-pattern only through Sentinel-2 is capped per administrative region at GASTAT 2024 wheat area minus the radar wheat already there: the cap goes first to (a)/(b) fields, then to (c) fields, pro rata by area. Water, energy and CO2 are not capped; energy uses the same pumping head as the radar-only totals, with pivot pressure decided by the tier's own class (none on its palm groves).",
